   "doc": "Records the next layer's L2 prefetch (its attention mix and input linears) behind the experts' gate / up instead of behind down, so it runs beside the network exchange and down and its weights are in L2 earlier. Measured on the Sparks' decode capture: the dense linears run 2x faster (wq_a + wkv 30 -> 15 us) when their prefetch had 80 us of lead, and 96 % of the standard placement's prefetches are still running when the consumer starts. On by default (the prefetch writes nothing); 2D decode windows on the native kernels only; 0 places it behind down. Replies unchanged.",
