   "label": "Drafter on a short vocabulary list",
   "doc": "The drafter proposes from a list of 32,768 token ids (8,192 on each node: the model's special tokens and the ids most frequent in the project's own text) instead of the whole vocabulary, so its output head reads about a sixteenth of the bytes and its Markov steps score a sixteenth of the columns. A draft is only a proposal the model checks, so replies are the model's own whatever the list holds; what the list changes is which tokens get proposed. A guard on rank 0 counts the committed tokens that fall outside the list and returns to the whole head while more than 2% of the last 4,096 do. On by default; set it to 0 to turn it off. Needs the four-node layout, TF_DS_DRAFT_HEAD=fp4 and the kernel kit's Markov kernels; where a rank cannot run it the start says so and every rank drafts from the whole head. Every node must agree.",
