   "label": "Fused attention epilogue kernel",
   "doc": "Which kit kernel the fused prompt attention epilogue (TF_DS_ATTN_EPI_FUSED) launches. ue is the standard kernel (_sparse_attn_part_ue). we runs ue's epilogue after w's mainloop (the latents' scale bytes read in the code bytes' layout, unpacked in place): measured x1.020 on prompts, replies byte-equal. xe is we, reading the next block's pick indices a block ahead and prefetching that block's rows into the GPU's first-level cache: x1.012, below we (its 21 register spills cost more than the prefetch saves). All three give the same bytes (the kernels replay compares them). It runs we unless set (a bit-identical speed change is on by default); a kit without the kernel keeps ue and says so in an 'off' line of the speed report. A value other than ue, we or xe refuses the start by name. Separate from TF_DS_ATTN_TWIN, which picks the decode and unfused calls' kernel.",
   "values": [
    "ue",
    "we",
    "xe"
   ],
   "seed": "name",
   "first_use": "families/dsv41/model.zig:2731",
   "secret": false
  },
