   ],
   "label": "Key tiles per index program",
   "doc": "How many 64-key tiles one program of a prompt chunk's index score takes in turn. 0 is the standard kernel. 4 uses the kernel kit's tile-looping build: the program reads its rows' queries, head weights and visible lengths once for the four tiles instead of once a tile, and prefetches the next tile's keys into the first-level cache; the same scores, keys and tile maxima (the kernels replay compares them). On by default (4): the kernel time measured on the Spark was 0.958 to 0.980 of the standard kernel's at the 9 shapes of a 4,096-row pass, the same bytes. 0 runs the standard kernel. Only 0 and 4 are built: another value refuses the start by name; a kit without the kernel leaves it off with a line saying why.",
   "values": [],
   "seed": "name",
