   "label": "Four-lane activation quantizer",
   "doc": "The activation quantizer (the front's input, wo_b's input, the experts' pack, wo_a's input rows) runs four lanes a 32-value group with 16-byte loads instead of a warp a group with 2-byte loads. The same bytes (every output byte equal to the standard kernel's over the prompt pass's shapes and fills with NaN, infinities, zeros and subnormals, kernels replay act_quant; measured on the Spark: 140 of 140 comparisons identical, the big prompt shapes x0.89 of the standard kernel's time, 1,024 rows x0.27 to x0.64), so it is on unless set to 0, which runs the standard kernel for every call. A call that is not bf16 or whose addresses or strides are not aligned runs the standard kernel either way. Any value but 0 or 1 refuses the start.",
