   ],
   "label": "Attention output groups in one launch",
   "doc": "A prompt chunk's wo_a on its FP8 rows (TF_DS_WOA_W8) runs both groups of a layer as one launch of the bf16-from-FP8 tile kernel (grid z = groups) instead of one launch a group. A group's launch is 256 tiles on 48 SMs, 5.33 waves, so 6 with the last one a third full; one launch over both is 10.67 waves, so 11: about one wave a layer by the wave arithmetic. Each tile runs its group's code unchanged, so the bytes are the group launches' (kernels replay woa_merge). On by default because of the kernel time measured on the Spark: a layer's wo_a took 0.945 of the two launches' time (null 0.998), about 2.1 ms of a 4,096-row pass, the same bytes (the wave estimate of 3.7 to 3.9 ms was high: the merge trims the tail wave, it does not remove it); 0 runs one launch a group. Any value but 0 or 1 refuses the start.",
   "values": [],
   "seed": "name",
   "first_use": "families/dsv41/model.zig:2493",
   "secret": false
  },
