   "label": "Exact split GEMMs on a 64-column tile",
   "doc": "With the exact-arithmetic matrix multiplies (TF_DS_MMA_SF_EXACT), a prompt chunk's wkv (512 columns) and wq_a (1,280 columns) run their split GEMMs on a 64 x 64 tile of 128 threads, two blocks an SM, instead of the 64 x 128 tile of 256 threads: their grids are 64 and 160 blocks on 48 SMs. A warp's 32 x 32 tile and every output element's K chain are the same, so the bytes are the 128-column tile's (kernels replay split64n); each rank decides for itself. On by default: at a 4,096-row pass's 1,024 owned rows the 64 x 64 tile takes 21.4 % less kernel time for wkv and 17.9 % less for wq_a (null control 0.0 %, measured on the Spark); 0 runs the 128-column tile.",
